---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Bubble Match — Privacy Policy">
  <section class="container-app py-12 max-w-3xl">
    <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold mb-2">Privacy Policy — Bubble Match</h1>
    <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400 mb-8">
      Last updated: <span class="notranslate">July 2, 2026</span>
    </p>

    <div class="prose dark:prose-invert space-y-6 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2">1. Overview</h2>
        <p>
          Bubble Match is a single-player offline game developed by Jacob. This policy
          explains what data the app handles.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2">2. Data we collect</h2>
        <p>
          <strong>Locally on your device:</strong> your game progress (high score,
          gems, power-ups, statistics) and your settings (sound, vibration, language).
          This data never leaves your device unless you choose to.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Through third-party advertising (Google AdMob):</strong> when an
          ad is shown, Google may collect a device advertising identifier, coarse
          (IP-based) location, device information, and ad interaction data. See
          section 4 below.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2">3. Permissions</h2>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-1">
          <li>
            <code class="notranslate">INTERNET</code> — required to fetch ads.
          </li>
          <li>
            <code class="notranslate">ACCESS_NETWORK_STATE</code> — used by the
            ad SDK to detect connectivity.
          </li>
          <li>
            <code class="notranslate">VIBRATE</code> — used for haptic feedback on
            bubble matches and game over.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2">4. Third-party services: Google AdMob</h2>
        <p>
          Bubble Match displays ads provided by
          <strong>Google AdMob</strong>. AdMob is operated by Google LLC and is
          subject to Google's own privacy practices.
        </p>
        <p>When an ad is loaded or shown, Google may automatically receive:</p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-1">
          <li>Your device's advertising identifier (Ad ID).</li>
          <li>Coarse location derived from your IP address.</li>
          <li>Device and app information (model, OS version, app version).</li>
          <li>Ad interaction data (impressions, clicks, video views).</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-2">For full details, read:</p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-1">
          <li>
            <a
              class="text-accent-600 dark:text-accent-400"
              href="https://policies.google.com/privacy"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Privacy Policy</a
            >.
          </li>
          <li>
            <a
              class="text-accent-600 dark:text-accent-400"
              href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer">How Google uses information from sites or
              apps that use our services</a
            >.
          </li>
          <li>
            <a
              class="text-accent-600 dark:text-accent-400"
              href="https://adssettings.google.com/"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer">Manage your ad personalization in Google
              Ads Settings</a
            >.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-2">
          You can reset or delete your device's advertising ID at any time from
          Android Settings &rarr; Google &rarr; Ads.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2">5. Children</h2>
        <p>
          The app is suitable for all ages. Google AdMob is configured to serve
          ads appropriate for all audiences. We do not knowingly collect personal
          data from children.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2">6. Your rights</h2>
        <p>
          You can erase all local data at any time by clearing the app's storage
          in Android Settings &rarr; Apps &rarr; Bubble Match &rarr; Storage &rarr;
          Clear data. For data Google has collected through ads, use Google's
          Ads Settings and Privacy controls linked above.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2">7. Changes to this policy</h2>
        <p>
          Any updates to this policy will be reflected on this page with a revised
          "Last updated" date.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2">8. Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Questions? Email
          <a
            class="text-accent-600 dark:text-accent-400 notranslate"
            href="mailto:kiktruedeveloper@gmail.com">kiktruedeveloper@gmail.com</a
          >.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
